invariant: INV-57
file: quic_config.c
catches: cnsa2_quic_test
reason: ch_quic_init drops the profile's pin refusal, which tls.c keeps,
  so a QUIC session of the profile stages a hello for a pinned config.
  test_cnsa2_quic_cfg requires CH_EINVAL with nothing staged.

--- old
    if (pin_ok && !CH_TAKES_PINS) {
--- new
    if (pin_ok && !CH_TAKES_PINS && 0) {
